Upstream models

This workflow sends a draft shipping document to a model endpoint that you configure and hold the
key for. The lab does not train, fine-tune or distribute models, and is not a provider of a
general-purpose AI model under the EU AI Act; obligations for the model itself rest with whoever
provides it, under their own terms.

A model is used for exactly one bounded job: copying the fields a requirement row names out of a
document, as written, with null where the document does not state a value. No model decides
whether a document is present, complete or correct. Presence is set arithmetic over the requirement
rows; agreement is a fixed comparison against the values a person typed on the Shipments row, and
swapping the model cannot change either.

Output produced through that endpoint is marked per Article 50. See COMPLIANCE.md.

---

Scope

The workflow checks a shipment's document pack against the shipping instruction, records a named
person's approval, and chases originals. It is not a letter of credit presentation tool, not a
freight or customs system, and it does not know whether the requirement rows you put in it are the
right ones for your contract.
